<p>A long-distance train crashed into the rear of a stopped commuter train late Monday at Bekasi Timur station in Bekasi, east of Jakarta, killing 15 people and injuring 88, Infrastructure Minister Agus Harimurti Yudhoyono said in an updated toll on Tuesday. Earlier figures from state railway operator PT Kereta Api Indonesia and rescue officials put the toll at 14 dead and 84 injured. The struck rear carriage was reserved for women, and several accounts said the fatalities were women riding in that section. Rescuers worked through the night and ended a nearly 12-hour operation Tuesday after cutting into crushed carriages; Mohammad Syafii, head of Basarnas, said no further victims were believed to remain in the wreckage. President Prabowo Subianto visited injured passengers in Bekasi and ordered an investigation into the collision. Officials said early findings indicated the commuter train first hit a taxi at a level crossing and stopped before the long-distance train struck it from behind, while police and the National Transportation Safety Committee investigated the cause.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vvgb-3inuhQagTlcUS7z5bCZ4dOrVUqPkQRTMMaDjJU0yKEd3wIHTUd2k49hKXt57aao0pgEBKU3O2fEx2lZrXPLSIXMDJis5pL7LuMwcIB7pee0fpK_4AoP-NswV8nwUzo-ilPe7eRCcmzwwdddi7jz6MHhEQ8cTHARJ_ALxi58z4CPYw4_xKNNsot0hnPivRj2ynbZZrhrhBJelPOadFGPw7LMVZiv5ooeF0Te2QUg2H7gu9sihQi8Vj90PCzfB14YUtgbN5g' alt='Technicians at the site after a deadly collision between a commuter line train and a long-distance train in Bekasi on the outskirts of Jakarta, Indonesia, on April 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Commuter context: Survivors told SCMP they were among workers heading from Jakarta to Cikarang after a long day at work when the train stopped at Bekasi Timur around 9 p.m..</li><li>Train passengers: Officials said all 240 people aboard the Argo Bromo Anggrek long-distance train were safe.</li><li>Exact timing: One early local account placed the collision at about 8:55 p.m. local time on April 27.</li><li>Route split: VietnamPlus described the long-distance train as operating on the Jakarta-Surabaya route and the commuter train on the Jakarta-Bekasi line.</li></ul><blockquote>I thought I was going to die - Sausan Sarifah</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Basarnas: Mohammad Syafii said rescuers needed specially trained personnel because some surviving passengers were pinned by train debris. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330457544/train-crash-near-jakarta-kills-14-dozens-trapped-as-rescue-continues'>Aaj TV</a>)</li><li>PT Kereta Api Indonesia: Chief executive Bobby Rasyidin said the company’s early account was preliminary and that investigators would establish the detailed accident chronology. (<a href='https://www.irishnews.com/news/world/train-crash-in-indonesia-leaves-14-women-dead-PMP3A5HGYJJUFOOLCLGL6XYOZY/'>The Irish News</a>)</li><li>President Prabowo Subianto: Prabowo linked a planned flyover near the tracks to chronic congestion around the crossing after visiting hospital patients. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330457544/train-crash-near-jakarta-kills-14-dozens-trapped-as-rescue-continues'>Aaj TV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/week-asia/people/article/3351713/survivors-describe-chaos-blood-and-twisted-metal-after-indonesia-train-crash-kills-15'>Survivors describe chaos, blood and twisted metal after Indonesia train crash kills 15</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckgegg8r0v1o'>Rescuers race to free survivors trapped inside train after fatal Indonesia crash</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/28/world/asia/indonesia-train-crash.html'>Trains Collide in Indonesia, Killing at Least 14 and Injuring Dozens</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995728/train-collision-kills-14-injures-dozens-near-jakarta'>Train collision kills 14, injures dozens near Jakarta</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.